Author: Átila Correia [aut, cre], Victor Lachos [aut], Carlos Diniz [ctb]
Maintainer: Átila Correia <atilapc1989@gmail.com>
Description: Tools for generating and estimating matrix-variate Normal (MVN) and 
    matrix-variate Skew-Normal (MVSN) models with or without interval censoring 
    and missing data. The package provides functions to simulate uncensored and 
    censored matrix-valued observations from MVN and MVSN distributions, as well 
    as routines for likelihood evaluation. Estimation procedures include maximum 
    likelihood for complete MVN data and EM-type algorithms for MVN and MVSN 
    models under interval censoring or missingness. Core functionality covers the 
    simulation of matrix-variate samples via the stochastic representation 
    X = M + A|Z| + V, and the generation of censored and uncensored data for 
    estimation.
